				\begin{document}$${{{{{{{\rm{q}}}}}}}}(c| {{{{{{{\bf{z}}}}}}}})=\frac{{\sum }_{{{{{{{{\rm{n}}}}}}}}=1}4{{{{{{{{\rm{q}}}}}}}}}_{{{{{{{{\rm{n}}}}}}}}}(c| {{{{{{{\bf{z}}}}}}}})}{4}$$\end{document}q(c∣z)=∑n=14qn(c∣z)4. We measure the algorithm performance on the unified test dataset. In Supplementary Table 2, we compare the different algorithms for estimating q(c∣z) in different iterations. The comparison shows that SVC with bootstrap yields the best result.

Details of the potential binder sampling process are given in Supplementary Methods 1 and 2. We consider a Gaussian distribution as the proposal distribution for \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
				\usepackage{wasysym} 
				\usepackage{amsfonts} 
				\usepackage{amssymb} 
